# NoSQL injection: user-controlled input (req.body / req.query / req.params)
# passed DIRECTLY into a MongoDB query filter object. Mongo treats an object
# like { _id: req.body.id } as a query — if req.body.id is itself an object
# (e.g. {"$ne": null}) the attacker controls the query operator (CWE-943).
#
# Found via OWASP Juice Shop's own author marker (2026-09-26):
#   routes/updateProductReviews.ts:18
#   db.reviewsCollection.update({ _id: req.body.id }, ...) // vuln-line noSqlReviewsChallenge
# keur had no NoSQL-injection rule at all (only KEUR-SQLI-* for classic SQL).
#
# Match a Mongo collection method (find/findOne/update/updateOne/delete*/remove/
# aggregate/count) whose FIRST argument object embeds req.body/query/params
# without a String()/sanitiser wrapper. A String(req.body.id) cast does not match.
id: KEUR-NOSQLI-001
ilities: [integrity]
maturity: 2
title: NoSQL injection — user input in a MongoDB query filter
category: sqli
severity: critical
engine: pattern
action: block
target:
  extensions: .js .ts .mjs
patterns:
  - regex: (?i)\.(?:find|findOne|findOneAndUpdate|update|updateOne|updateMany|deleteOne|deleteMany|remove|count|countDocuments|aggregate)\s*\(\s*\{[^}]*\breq\.(?:body|query|params)\.[A-Za-z0-9_]+[^}]*\}
    exclude: (?i)(?:String|Number|parseInt|parseFloat|Boolean|ObjectId)\s*\(\s*req\.(?:body|query|params)|\{\s*where\s*:
    message: A MongoDB query filter embeds req.body/query/params directly (CWE-943). If the value is an object the attacker controls the query operators (e.g. {"$ne":null}) — NoSQL injection. Cast/validate the value (String(req.body.id)) or use a schema-validated, typed query.
confidence: 0.8
fix: Coerce and validate the input before it reaches the query — e.g. { _id: String(req.body.id) } — or use a validation layer (Joi/zod) so a query operator object can never be injected.
